{
  "id": "e095a100-d028-4bbb-a175-a6886137df61",
  "title": "Implement general Galois field GF(p^m) arithmetic",
  "description": "Implement prime field arithmetic for GF(p) and general extension fields GF(p^m). This is the foundational algebraic expansion from GF(2)/GF(2^m) to a general-purpose finite field toolkit.\n\nSee linked design documents for detailed architecture.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- **Trait hierarchy**: `FiniteField` + `ConstField` + `FiniteFieldExt` implemented and proven across `Gf2mElement`, `Fp<P>`, `Gf2_8`/`Gf2_16`, and `QuadraticExt<F>`\n- **Wide accumulator**: Associated `Wide` type on `FiniteField` for bounds-aware delayed reduction, enabling generic matrix kernels to accumulate without field-specific code (inspired by fflas-ffpack's `MMHelper` pattern)\n- **FieldVec**: Generic `FieldVec<F>` with scalar and SIMD-accelerated operations, including delayed-reduction dot product with bounds-aware scheduling\n- **Axiom tests**: All trait implementations pass property-based field axiom test harness (associativity, commutativity, distributivity, characteristic, inverse, hash consistency)\n- **Linear algebra readiness**: Trait expressiveness and kernel performance proven sufficient to support generic `FieldMatrix` linear algebra — the downstream linear algebra epic can build directly on this foundation without trait changes\n- **Performance**: Zero-overhead abstraction for const-generic types; competitive with fflas-ffpack element-level throughput for prime field arithmetic\n\n## References\n\n- [fflas-ffpack analysis](dev/plans/fflas_ffpack_analysis.md) — design patterns and benchmark targets\n- [GF(p^n) groundwork analysis](dev/plans/gfpn_groundwork_analysis.md) — trait hierarchy and build order\n- [GF(p^n) planning session](dev/plans/gfpn_planning_session.md) — architecture exploration",
